{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Posiya","html":"<article id='thag1.34'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.34 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.34 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catutthavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Four </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Posiyattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Posiya </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Anāsannavarā etā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It’s always better for a smart person </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccameva vijānatā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>to avoid sharing a seat with such women. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Gāmā araññamāgamma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I went from the village to the wilderness; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tato gehaṁ upāvisi; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>from there I entered a house. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tato uṭṭhāya pakkāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Though I was there to be fed, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>anāmantetvā posiyo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I got up and left without taking leave. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Posiyo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
